From 33128a948af9febe197a556e1d9cd0e013e6197d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:46:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: mediatek: mt6797-vdec: add H.264 decoding

Program the MT6797 video decoder for progressive 8-bit 4:2:0 H.264
(Baseline, Main and High) through the V4L2 stateless H.264 API, next to
the existing HEVC path. As for HEVC there is no firmware: for every
picture the CPU resets the core, reads the first slice header through
the hardware bit reader, programs the SPS, PPS, slice, POC and initial
reference list registers from the controls and the v4l2-h264 list
helpers, lets the hardware parse the list modifications and weight
tables, and starts one decode for all slices of the picture.

Frame-based decoding with Annex-B start codes only. The register
sequence comes from reverse engineering and has not been compared with
a hardware trace yet.
